I love dark and Stormies I mean who does  it's a great summer drink but I've  always wanted to enjoy something like it  all year around so I thought it would be  cool to do a variation on it for the  Fall incorporating some of those  trademark autumnal flavors and today I'm  going to show it to you it's called The  Tempest for this cocktail you're gonna  need some apple brandy some fresh lime  juice and some fresh ginger cinnamon  syrup and some hard apple cider or hard  pumpkin cider we're gonna build this  drink in a mixing glass shake it up and  strand it over a highball glass later to  start we're going to muddle some fresh  ginger in with our cinnamon syrup  cinnamon syrup is the ultimate fall  cocktail ingredient you do have to make  yourself but it's a cinch and really  worth the effort all you have to do is  crush up about six cinnamon sticks add  about two cups of simple syrup bring the  whole thing to a boil then take it right  off heat and then let it sit for about  six to twelve hours then strain out the  cinnamon it works with whiskey works  with gin works with champagne got tons  of uses you won't regret it  okay got our ginger and cinnamon in  there now we're gonna juice some limes  just half an ounce fresh lime juice and  then one ounce of apple brandy apple  brandy is distilled apples there are a  lot of versions out there you might have  heard of Calvados which is also an apple  brandy from Calvados France it's a  little bit rounder I prefer the more  American versions that are sharper more  whiskey alright now we're going to shake  this and strain into a highball glass  and I like to use a fine strainer to get  those little bits of ginger nice even  texture and now instead of ginger beer  like a traditional darkness for me we're  gonna top it with hard apple cider or if  you're lucky and a fall a lot of  producers release a pumpkin cider which  is amazing in this drink both are great  though top it off and finally we're  gonna garnish with a lime wheel and a  cinnamon stick and that is the tempest  this is a great drink for Halloween  parties your costume will not be  complete without one if you like that  recipe tell us some of your favorite  drinks you like to make at home in the  comments below and subscribe to the GQ  channel we've got lots more of them
 

